---

# 🏫 Insertion at Any Position in Linked List

---

### 🔹 Concept
To insert at position `pos`:
1. If `pos == 1` → it’s just insert at start.
2. Else → traverse to the `(pos-1)`th node.
3. Create a new node.
4. Link new node’s `next` to `(pos-1)->next`.
5. Update `(pos-1)->next = newNode`.

---

### 🔹 Code

```c
struct Node* insertAtPos(struct Node* head, int value, int pos) {
    struct Node* newNode = (struct Node*)malloc(sizeof(struct Node));
    newNode->data = value;
    newNode->next = NULL;

    // Case 1: Insert at start
    if (pos == 1) {
        newNode->next = head;
        head = newNode;
        return head;
    }

    // Case 2: Insert in middle or end
    struct Node* temp = head;
    for (int i = 1; i < pos-1 && temp != NULL; i++) {
        temp = temp->next;
    }

    if (temp == NULL) {
        printf("Position out of range!\n");
        free(newNode);
        return head;
    }

    newNode->next = temp->next;
    temp->next = newNode;

    return head;
}
```

---

### 🔹 Dry Run Example
List = `10 → 20 → 30 → NULL`  
Insert `15` at position `2`.

1. Traverse to node at pos-1 = 1 (`10`).  
2. Link newNode (15) → next of temp (20).  
3. Link temp (10) → newNode.  

Final:  
`10 → 15 → 20 → 30 → NULL`

---

# 🏫 Deletion at Any Position in Linked List

---

### 🔹 Concept
To delete at position `pos`:
1. If `pos == 1` → it’s just delete at start.
2. Else → traverse to `(pos-1)`th node.
3. Save pointer to node to delete = `(pos-1)->next`.
4. Update `(pos-1)->next = toDelete->next`.
5. Free the `toDelete` node.

---

### 🔹 Code

```c
struct Node* deleteAtPos(struct Node* head, int pos) {
    if (head == NULL) return NULL;

    // Case 1: Delete first node
    if (pos == 1) {
        struct Node* temp = head;
        head = head->next;
        free(temp);
        return head;
    }

    // Case 2: Delete in middle or end
    struct Node* temp = head;
    for (int i = 1; i < pos-1 && temp != NULL; i++) {
        temp = temp->next;
    }

    if (temp == NULL || temp->next == NULL) {
        printf("Position out of range!\n");
        return head;
    }

    struct Node* toDelete = temp->next;
    temp->next = toDelete->next;
    free(toDelete);

    return head;
}
```

---

### 🔹 Dry Run Example
List = `10 → 20 → 30 → 40 → NULL`  
Delete at position `3`.

1. Traverse to node at pos-1 = 2 (`20`).  
2. `toDelete = 20->next` = node with `30`.  
3. Update `20->next = 30->next` (i.e., `40`).  
4. Free node `30`.  

Final:  
`10 → 20 → 40 → NULL`

---

# 🧠 Key Tricks (Exam Tips)
- Use `pos == 1` to reduce to “insert/delete at start” → saves code repetition.  
- In `for` loop → always stop at `(pos-1)`th node, not `pos`.  
- Always check **position validity** (`temp == NULL` or `temp->next == NULL`).  
- Draw diagrams with 3–4 nodes in exams — instant clarity + marks.  

