# 🔹 Insert at Position (1 to N)

```c
struct Node* insertAtPos(struct Node* head, int value, int pos) {
    struct Node* newNode = (struct Node*)malloc(sizeof(struct Node));
    newNode->data = value;
    newNode->next = NULL;

    // Case: Insert at start
    if (pos == 1) {
        newNode->next = head;
        head = newNode;
        return head;
    }

    // Traverse to (pos-1)th node
    struct Node* temp = head;
    for (int i = 1; i < pos-1 && temp != NULL; i++) {
        temp = temp->next;
    }

    // If position is out of range
    if (temp == NULL) {
        printf("Position out of range!\n");
        free(newNode);
        return head;
    }

    // Link new node
    newNode->next = temp->next;
    temp->next = newNode;

    return head;
}
```

✅ Works for:
- `pos = 1` → Insert at start  
- `pos = length+1` → Insert at end  
- `pos in middle` → Insert in between  

---

# 🔹 Delete at Position (1 to N)

```c
struct Node* deleteAtPos(struct Node* head, int pos) {
    if (head == NULL) {
        printf("List is empty!\n");
        return NULL;
    }

    // Case: Delete first node
    if (pos == 1) {
        struct Node* temp = head;
        head = head->next;
        free(temp);
        return head;
    }

    // Traverse to (pos-1)th node
    struct Node* temp = head;
    for (int i = 1; i < pos-1 && temp != NULL; i++) {
        temp = temp->next;
    }

    // Check if position is valid
    if (temp == NULL || temp->next == NULL) {
        printf("Position out of range!\n");
        return head;
    }

    // Delete the node
    struct Node* toDelete = temp->next;
    temp->next = toDelete->next;
    free(toDelete);

    return head;
}
```

✅ Works for:
- `pos = 1` → Delete start  
- `pos = length` → Delete end  
- `pos in middle` → Delete middle  

---

# 🔑 Why This Works (Professor-Style)

- In both insert & delete:  
  → You always traverse to the **(pos-1)th node**.  
  → Because only that node can safely “rewire” its `next` pointer.  

- Edge cases handled:
  - `pos == 1` → Special: head pointer changes.  
  - `pos > length` → Invalid, prevent crash.  
  - `pos == length+1` in insert → Equivalent to inserting at end.  

