# 🏫 What is a Doubly Linked List?

In a DLL, **each node has two pointers**:  
- `prev` → points to the previous node  
- `next` → points to the next node  

### Node structure in C:
```c
struct Node {
    int data;
    struct Node* prev;
    struct Node* next;
};
```

So memory looks like this:

```
NULL <- [data | prev | next] <-> [data | prev | next] <-> [data | prev | next] -> NULL
```

✅ Advantage over SLL:  
- You can move both **forward** and **backward**.  
- Deletion at end or middle doesn’t require traversing the whole list to find the previous node — you already have `prev`.  

---

# 🔹 Traversal in DLL

### Forward Traversal
```c
void printForward(struct Node* head) {
    struct Node* temp = head;
    while (temp != NULL) {
        printf("%d <-> ", temp->data);
        temp = temp->next;
    }
    printf("NULL\n");
}
```

### Backward Traversal
```c
void printBackward(struct Node* tail) {
    struct Node* temp = tail;
    while (temp != NULL) {
        printf("%d <-> ", temp->data);
        temp = temp->prev;
    }
    printf("NULL\n");
}
```

👉 Here, we need to keep track of both `head` (for forward) and `tail` (for backward).

---

# 🔹 Insert in DLL

### Insert at Start
```c
struct Node* insertAtStart(struct Node* head, int value) {
    struct Node* newNode = (struct Node*)malloc(sizeof(struct Node));
    newNode->data = value;
    newNode->prev = NULL;
    newNode->next = head;

    if (head != NULL)
        head->prev = newNode;

    head = newNode;
    return head;
}
```

---

### Insert at End
```c
struct Node* insertAtEnd(struct Node* head, int value) {
    struct Node* newNode = (struct Node*)malloc(sizeof(struct Node));
    newNode->data = value;
    newNode->next = NULL;

    if (head == NULL) {
        newNode->prev = NULL;
        return newNode;
    }

    struct Node* temp = head;
    while (temp->next != NULL) {
        temp = temp->next;
    }

    temp->next = newNode;
    newNode->prev = temp;

    return head;
}
```

---

### Insert at Position
```c
struct Node* insertAtPos(struct Node* head, int value, int pos) {
    struct Node* newNode = (struct Node*)malloc(sizeof(struct Node));
    newNode->data = value;

    if (pos == 1) {
        newNode->prev = NULL;
        newNode->next = head;
        if (head != NULL) head->prev = newNode;
        return newNode;
    }

    struct Node* temp = head;
    for (int i = 1; i < pos-1 && temp != NULL; i++) {
        temp = temp->next;
    }

    if (temp == NULL) {
        printf("Position out of range!\n");
        free(newNode);
        return head;
    }

    newNode->next = temp->next;
    newNode->prev = temp;

    if (temp->next != NULL)
        temp->next->prev = newNode;

    temp->next = newNode;

    return head;
}
